{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229689-how-will-the-gehenna-war-end","id":1229689,"title":"How Will the Gehenna War End?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-23T18:08:39-07:00","id":1229689,"title":"How Will the Gehenna War End?","content":"So. Let's make list about what we know of the Sabbat in Vampire The Masquerade Fifth Edition<br /> <br /> 1-They will be scarier than ever according to the Gentleman Gamer<br /> 2-They are on the Middle East fighting the Gehenna War for the Graves of antedilluvians according to Martin Ericson.<br /> <br /> Today i asked about the Lasombra on White Wolf's facebook page,they were very polite and told me &quot;Sabbat is not covered in the core book (focusing on camarilla vs. anarch), so you will have to wait until the Cainites return from the gehenna crusade to find out how the Lasombra have changed.&quot; Now,it might be nothing however they <i>did </i>said the will <i>return </i>from the Gehenna Crusade.<br /> How will they change then? Will one of them be back with an Third Generation vampire's soul on his body? Will one of the antedilluvians awaken before the Sabbat manage to eat them an destroy the Sect?<br /> <br /> Maybe,i should ask,what do <i>y'all </i>plan to do with the Gehenna Crusade,after all it was said our chronicles would dictate the Metaplot from now on,what do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T18:10:44-07:00","id":1229691,"title":"","content":"Mods,would you mind moving this to the VTM forum?i forgot to put in there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 06-23-2018, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T00:46:26-07:00","id":1229756,"title":"","content":"I have no idea about how the Lasombra will change but I really hope they'll go from blatant thugs to more &quot;manipulative shadows&quot; or &quot;dark priests&quot;. So essentially I'm hoping for them to get more focused as a Clan concept. Replacing Obteneration with Obfuscate would be an instant point from me but maybe that's so entrenched that it can't be touched without a general player uprising.<br /> <br /> But then again I'm mostly interested in the historical settings for the game, and as of now the Victorian Age setting, so I don't think that my chronicle will affect much if anything regardless of how the new metaplot would take in player input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T11:12:54-08:00","id":1265018,"title":"","content":"The war in the 5th edition where the Sabbat are gathering en masse to destroy the Antedilluvians in the Middle East? If I had to guess, I would say that the Sabbat would have a glorious crusade, but would end up getting exterminated in the process. Basically it is a contest of Sabbat vampires which are mostly of Ancillae and Neonate status, against vampires that have godlike power. Sure numbers and AK 47's count for a great deal, but the tools that the 3rd Generation has at their disposal would be too great. Add to the fact that Elders around the world are being summoned to protect the 3rd Generation and I would forecast a lot of dead Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T11:20:11-08:00","id":1265024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229689-how-will-the-gehenna-war-end?p=1265018#post1265018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The war in the 5th edition where the Sabbat are gathering en masse to destroy the Antedilluvians in the Middle East? If I had to guess, I would say that the Sabbat would have a glorious crusade, but would end up getting exterminated in the process. Basically it is a contest of Sabbat vampires which are mostly of Ancillae and Neonate status, against vampires that have godlike power. Sure numbers and AK 47's count for a great deal, but the tools that the 3rd Generation has at their disposal would be too great. Add to the fact that Elders around the world are being summoned to protect the 3rd Generation and I would forecast a lot of dead Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is possible,personally I'd prefer something else","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T11:31:05-08:00","id":1265030,"title":"","content":"I'd bet on the Sabbat becoming a smaller group, with independently operating religious terrorist cells and without higher command or holdings. Most of their elders lost in the war, the remaining ancillae and neonates becoming disenfranchised or frightened and coming back with a haunting in their eyes.<br /> <br /> So, a mix of 1e Sabbat and Belial's Brood/VII from Requiem. I'm not counting on anything like the Sabbat from 2e-Revised-V20.<br /> <br /> At least that's what I think the material we're already having points to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T15:33:19-08:00","id":1265134,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go the other way. They will become like being Nephandus for Vampires. They aren't &quot;just a sect you can defect to&quot; you go through the rites and it changes you into something else. They will take up much of the workload of the Lupines for keeping cities broken and isolated because they break the rules show up and shatter places. They will take up some of the aspect of KOTE their domains are poorly infiltraited because they aren't playing the same games.<br /> <br /> We will thus see Fiends, Not Giovanni, and Ravnos in a faction for the last playable groups to give the full 13 options of clans. The Sabbat will be functionally a separate game that crossover like KOTE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T05:53:31-08:00","id":1265248,"title":"","content":"I have a really hard time believing that the Gehenna Crusade is just going to end and the survivors are just going to come home. It was advertised as one of the two primary metaplot elements of V5, and it would be wholly disappointing if we just settled back into some sort of North American status quo. I really have no idea what is going on with the Lasombra, but that aside, I think the Sabbat book will give us a fully playable Crusade setting and perhaps information on the limited number of Sabbat that stayed behind in their domains.<br /> <br /> I certainly hope, and don't think, they are going to become a pure Nephandi-esque adversary. Vampire has always, ALWAYS, presented the Antediluvians as bad news, and now we officially know that the Camarilla works on their behalf. So however scary the Sabbat may be, I still think you will be able to make a moral case for them. That may just be wishful thinking on my part, because they are my favourite sect. But honestly, reading the Gehenna War fiction from the Camarilla book, I would be very interested to play in that environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24186-emmameta","user":"emmameta","date":". 11-07-2018, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24186-emmameta","name":"emmameta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T12:31:49-08:00","id":1265354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmameta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229689-how-will-the-gehenna-war-end?p=1265248#post1265248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a really hard time believing that the Gehenna Crusade is just going to end and the survivors are just going to come home. It was advertised as one of the two primary metaplot elements of V5, and it would be wholly disappointing if we just settled back into some sort of North American status quo. I really have no idea what is going on with the Lasombra, but that aside, I think the Sabbat book will give us a fully playable Crusade setting and perhaps information on the limited number of Sabbat that stayed behind in their domains.<br /> <br /> I certainly hope, and don't think, they are going to become a pure Nephandi-esque adversary. Vampire has always, ALWAYS, presented the Antediluvians as bad news, and now we officially know that the Camarilla works on their behalf. So however scary the Sabbat may be, I still think you will be able to make a moral case for them. That may just be wishful thinking on my part, because they are my favourite sect. But honestly, reading the Gehenna War fiction from the Camarilla book, I would be very interested to play in that environment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant the Nephandi as an example of a transition of type that you can't just jump back to. You can't &quot;Defect&quot; from Nephandi you've changed what you are. I didnt mean that the Sabbat would be unplayable just it would be as different as playing a KJ now.<br /> <br /> The Rites and paths change you thus why the Lasombra who seemed to be more paying lipservice to the ideals seem to have defected. I don't think &quot;The sabbat is just another sect and you move your touchstones around like so...&quot; will have the same impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T14:42:27-08:00","id":1265387,"title":"","content":"I'm really interested to see what, if anything, they do with the Paths. The core morality system already allows you to create a pretty inhuman monster if you wanted to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24186-emmameta","name":"emmameta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T20:43:08-08:00","id":1265438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmameta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229689-how-will-the-gehenna-war-end?p=1265387#post1265387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really interested to see what, if anything, they do with the Paths. The core morality system already allows you to create a pretty inhuman monster if you wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From what we get from the other guides is they are meant to be different and scary. So I imagine whatever path equivalents survive though its more Metamorphosis and less. Honorable Accord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T21:09:33-08:00","id":1265447,"title":"","content":"Well, with the Tzimisce undisputed leaders now, that would stand to reason. But still, I hope there is room for other moralities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24186-emmameta","name":"emmameta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T11:04:16-08:00","id":1265530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmameta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229689-how-will-the-gehenna-war-end?p=1265447#post1265447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, with the Tzimisce undisputed leaders now, that would stand to reason. But still, I hope there is room for other moralities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think whatever they will be on will be as broad as Humanity in v5 is.. its just going to be sufficiently different that you couldn't put it in the base book. Like how v5 humanity can cover Honorable Accord, Typhon etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T13:47:16-08:00","id":1265567,"title":"","content":"Maybe after the crusade the Sabbat are even more undisputed sock puppets to the Antes. Maybe specific Antes start claiming specific Sabbat Factions. I mean how can they expect to beat them when their strongest get Beckoned by plot device?<br /> <br /> Also this should be in the Vampire Forum.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I\u2019m really curious about is the Tal\u2019mahe\u2019rah. Maybe the Sabbat gets absorbed by the True Black Hand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T21:33:26-08:00","id":1266342,"title":"","content":"With a whimper, not a bang <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T09:59:28-08:00","id":1269599,"title":"","content":"When asked how it will end, Kosh said &quot;In fire.&quot; He also said if we go to the First City, we will die, but he pronounced the name oddly.<br /> <br /> In any case, I doubt any of the books will present a formal end to the Gehenna War. In the WoD I expect more turmoil across the Near, Middle and Far East. It might even see a collapse to the Masquerade, or at least the start of a process to the collapse of the masquerade. The Gehenna War would destroy many of the vampires supporting the 3rd generation. And lets be clear here; the Sabbat are the tools of at least the Tzimisce founder, and possibly the Lesombra founder as well. There will be considerable damage to all those involved in the war, with the exception of the 3rd generation themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}